# AES-128 GCM encrypt vectors, from NIST's Cryptographic Algorithm Validation
# Program. Used here only for the GHASH chain, which is arithmetic in the same
# GF(2^128) this crate implements.
#
#   source:  https://csrc.nist.gov/CSRC/media/Projects/Cryptographic-Algorithm-Validation-Program/documents/mac/gcmtestvectors.zip
#   sha256:  f9fc479e134cde2980b3bb7cddbcb567b2cd96fd753835243ed067699f26a023
#   file:    gcmEncryptExtIV128.rsp  (CAVS 14.0, generated 2012-08-31)
#   subset:  every [IVlen = 96] group, first 3 counts each -- 175 groups, 525
#            cases. The 96-bit-IV form is the one where the counter block is
#            IV || 0^31 || 1, so GHASH is recoverable from the tag without
#            running the whole of GCM.
#
# Retrieved 2026-07-28. Not edited beyond the selection above.

